 * Drives the pushed stock-detail screen. This is the first `SavedStateHandle`-driven ViewModel in
 * this codebase — every other pushed screen either takes no argument (News, whose "which article"
 * signal is hoisted `remember` state in `PulseNavGraph`, not a nav arg) or a directly-encoded path
 * segment read straight off the nav backstack entry in the composable (`webview/{encodedUrl}`).
 * A per-symbol detail screen is a better fit for the standard Hilt pattern: `hiltViewModel()`
 * inside a `composable("${ROUTE_STOCK_DETAIL}/{$ARG_SYMBOL}") { ... }` destination auto-populates
 * `SavedStateHandle[ARG_SYMBOL]` from the route, and a distinct route string per symbol
 * (`stock_detail/AAPL` vs `stock_detail/MSFT`) means Compose Navigation gives each open symbol its
 * own ViewModel instance scoped to that backstack entry — exactly the "no default selection,
 * fetch this one symbol" shape the old chip-selection code had, without needing to hand-roll it.
 *
 * No `SyncManager` here — per `StockAnalysisRepository`'s interface doc, detail is deliberately
 * NOT sync-flag-driven; it's fetched on demand and `refreshDetail` already skips the network when
 * the cached detail's `detailVersion` matches the cached preview's. `onStart()` is kept anyway
 * (rather than firing the fetch from `init {}`) purely so the future Route's lifecycle wiring is
 * identical to every other screen's `DisposableEffect` — `onStop()` is intentionally a no-op.
